thinking_content: '**Hybrid Optimization Prioritization**


  Okay, here''s the plan. I''m aiming to surpass my best-ever MSHC score by optimizing the hybrid approach. The previous run (ID 827) underperformed, and the GA phase seems to be the bottleneck. I''m focusing on the trade-off between the GA''s exploration and the MSHC''s refinement. My core idea is that the GA''s current parameters might be too aggressive, leading to mediocre starting points for the MSHC phase. It seems that while MSHC excels at local search, GA isn''t setting it up for success.


  So, here''s what I''ll do. First, I''ll keep the GA parameters from my successful runs - specifically, a population size of 100, a mutation rate of 0.1, and an initial mutation strength of 0.05. These values have worked well in previous experiments. But I am reducing the GA budget to 400 seconds, leaving more time for MSHC. Then, with the extra time, I am reinstating the original 5 MSHC refinement runs. This will allow the MSHC phase more cycles to work. The aim is to make the GA phase generate better seeds for MSHC, and the MSHC phase is being given a larger time budget to produce better results.


  By tweaking the time allocation in this way, I''m trying to ensure that the GA phase focuses on generating diverse solutions, while the MSHC phase hones the best solution even further. The goal is to surpass my best-ever score with this adjusted hybrid.  Let''s see if this improved time allocation works.

  '
