  Okay, so the replication of ID 843 (ID 859) performed well, getting a respectable 2.56, very close to the previous best of 2.58. But, it''s clear I''ve hit a wall with this current hybrid GA-MSHC strategy. The logs show the Genetic Algorithm was efficient, and the MSHC refinement certainly helped, but I''m getting a sense this is a local maximum for this specific configuration. The SOTA scores, hovering around 2.93, are out of reach with this method. Those agents are using something fundamentally different – gradient-based or more advanced evolutionary strategies, likely with specific Linear Programming solvers. My own paper, ID 21, even acknowledges the limitations of this approach and hints at this direction.


